# S-044 quirk Q: a callback may disconnect inputs while the thread iterates over them (the input mutex is
# recursive). Removal shifts the array, and the iteration index still advances, so the input that moved into the
# vacated index is skipped for that frame.
vopen v I420 30 1 16 8 3
vconnect v a 1
vconnect v a 2
vconnect v a 3
vhook a 1 disconnect_self
vlock v 1 1 0x01
vunlock v
vinputs v
vlock v 1 2 0x02
vunlock v
# disconnect an input that sits earlier in the list than the one running
vconnect v b 4
vhook b 4 disconnect a 2
vlock v 1 3 0x03
vunlock v
vinputs v
vclose v
